    "stem": "Kabir rewrites $5x+8=2x+20$ in the form $Ax+B=Cx+D$ and then uses $x=\\dfrac{D-B}{A-C}$.\n\nWhich claim correctly identifies the values and the solution?",
    "item_type": "mcq",
    "options": {
      "A": "Call the answer the letter $B$ alone, and stop.",
      "B": "Use $x=\\dfrac{D-B}{A-C}$ even when the equation is not first put in $Ax+B=Cx+D$ form.",
      "C": "$A=5$, $B=8$, $C=2$, $D=20$, so $x=\\dfrac{20-8}{5-2}=4$.",
      "D": "Say that dividing for $x$ is what creates the $Ax+B=Cx+D$ layout of the equation."
    },
